  "properties": {
    "title": "deegree - Server-side open source software for the geospatial web",
    "description": "The OSGeo project deegree is server-side open source software for spatial data infrastructures (SDI) and the geospatial web. It implements standards of the Open Geospatial Consortium (OGC) and the ISO Technical Committee 211. The project hosts official reference implementations of OGC standards such as OGC API - Features, WFS, WMS and GML.\r\n\r\nThis talk will give an overview of the latest release 3.6 as well as recent developments of version 3.7 featuring support of Java 21 and Tomcat 11. Additionally, the deegree implementation of the OGC API - Features standard will be presented.\r\n\r\nLastly, future directions and planned core developments of the project will be highlighted.",
